remote-mocial/

# Not referenced by any page, and this repo publishes to mocial.org via
# GitHub Pages - anything committed here is fetchable at mocial.org/<file>.
# Delete a line to start tracking that file again.
#
# Letter.pdf and PHD_purpose_of_intent.pdf were here until the college folder
# started linking them. They are deliberately public now.
IMG_6959.heic
Patent_Application_Filed.DOCX

# Unreferenced and heavy - not worth the repo weight until something uses them
snaplogoglitch.MOV
twitterbot/

# Design reference only (the Win95 dialog the password gate is modelled on).
# Nothing on the site loads these - delete this line if something starts to.
windows-95-app-icons/

# The converter's log of what has been converted. This one matters: per the
# note at the top, anything committed here is fetchable at mocial.org/<file>,
# and a database of every link run through the converter is not something to
# publish by accident. converter/server.py itself is fine to track - it's just
# code - but the database it writes is not.
converter/conversions.db
converter/*.db
converter/*.db-journal

# Converted audio and video, if you ever point MOCIAL_CONVERTER_DIR at the
# project folder instead of /tmp. Same reasoning, more so.
converter/files/

# Commercial recording, kept local. The tray clock plays it off your own disk;
# committing it would publish it at mocial.org/<file> and put it in the repo's
# history, where deleting it later means a rewrite rather than a delete.
# Coeursica.mp3 and Howl are deliberately public - they aren't this.
Pink Floyd - Time (No Intro⧸No Clocks).mp3
